Typedef
-------

* Typedef is one of the datatype which is used to provide another name to existing datatype. 
* To make understanding of variable or datatype easy. 

syntax : 

	typedef old_datatype_name new_name;

Note: Newname should not be any keyword 


/* 
	#include <stdio.h>
	typedef int INTEGER;
	void main() {
		
		INTEGER i;
		printf("%d\n", sizeof(i));	// 4
	}

*/

